@startuml
title CycleFar — Propose and apply a feedback adaptation

autonumber
hide footbox

actor Rider
boundary "Owner-scoped\nRails controllers" as Controller
control "WorkoutBuilder" as Materializer
control "CompletionRecorder" as Recorder
control "FeedbackEvaluator" as Evaluator
control "ProposalCreator +\nProposalFreshness" as Freshness
control "ProposalComparison" as Comparison
control "FeedbackLoadLimiter" as Limiter
control "WeeklyLoadCap +\nLoadReduction" as LoadRules
control "ProposalApplier" as Applier
control "ManualEditor" as Editor
database "PostgreSQL" as Database

== Complete an executable workout and decide whether to propose ==
Rider -> Controller: POST completion with RPE and quality
Controller -> Database: load rider-owned planned executable workout
Controller -> Recorder: call(workout)
group completion transaction under plan lock
  Recorder -> Database: lock plan; reload and validate source
  opt source is a due/overdue outline
    Recorder -> Materializer: build_for_completion!(source)
    Materializer -> Database: read source context and fixed weekly load
    Materializer -> Materializer: generate source definition at current FTP with saved choices
    Materializer -> LoadRules: fit only source against context and weekly load
    Materializer -> Database: save source steps, profile and generation choices
  end
  Recorder -> Database: save feedback; read current owner FTP
  Recorder -> Recorder: recalculate metrics from canonical steps
  Recorder -> Database: mark completed; freeze FTP, watts, metrics and feedback
  Recorder -> Evaluator: evaluate feedback
  opt regular workout
    opt source is overdue
      Evaluator -> Database: read next scheduled workout for late-feedback guard
    end
    Evaluator -> Evaluator: evaluate RPE/quality if late-feedback guard permits
    opt feedback warrants an adjustment
      Evaluator -> Database: read comparable planned structured targets in today..day 13
      opt proposed target changes exist
        Evaluator -> Comparison: preview unsaved candidate (skip freshness validation)
        Comparison -> Limiter: fit targets within ceilings and weekly load
        Limiter -> Editor: preview canonical changes at current FTP
        Editor --> Limiter: definitions and metrics
        Limiter -> LoadRules: apply ordered reductions against comparable hard week
        LoadRules --> Limiter: load-limited definitions, retaining profile and duration
        Limiter --> Comparison: proposed prescriptions
        Comparison --> Evaluator: current/proposed metrics
        Evaluator -> Evaluator: remove no-op or wrong-direction changes
        opt meaningful changes remain
          Evaluator --> Recorder: reason, target payload and optional global bias
          Recorder -> Freshness: ProposalCreator.create!(evaluation)
          Freshness -> Database: capture relevant canonical-input digest
          Freshness -> Database: save proposal with seven-day expiry and digest
        end
      end
    end
  end
end
Controller --> Rider: redirect to calendar

== Review: comparison itself is read-only ==
Rider -> Controller: GET calendar
Controller -> Materializer: materialize eligible today..day 13 outlines
Materializer -> LoadRules: recheck actual generated load; retain sampled profiles
Materializer -> Database: save only new structures and load references
Controller -> Database: load this rider's pending proposals
Controller -> Comparison: calculate Current / Proposed values
Comparison -> Freshness: validate expiry, active plan and canonical-input digest
Freshness -> Database: read relevant owner-scoped canonical inputs
alt fresh proposal and valid planned structured targets in today..day 13
  Comparison -> Limiter: recheck target set, ceilings and weekly load
  Limiter -> LoadRules: ordered reductions against fixed load and forecasts
  Limiter --> Comparison: in-memory bounded prescriptions
  Comparison --> Controller: before/after workouts and clamped bias
  Controller --> Rider: show comparison and Accept / Reject
else expired, stale, legacy or invalid proposal
  Comparison --> Controller: unavailable with dismissal guidance
  Controller --> Rider: show Reject only
end

== Decision ==
alt Reject (available or unavailable)
  Rider -> Controller: DELETE proposal
  Controller -> Database: load rider-owned proposal
  Controller -> Applier: reject!
  Applier -> Database: lock plan, then proposal; destroy proposal
else Accept
  Rider -> Controller: POST accept proposal
  Controller -> Database: load rider-owned proposal
  Controller -> Applier: accept!
  group acceptance transaction: lock plan, then proposal
    Applier -> Database: lock owned plan and proposal
    Applier -> Freshness: revalidate expiry and canonical inputs
    Freshness -> Database: read current canonical context
    alt unavailable or target validation fails
      Applier --> Controller: error; roll back edits and preserve proposal
    else available
      Applier -> Comparison: revalidate freshness and calculate whole target set
      Comparison -> Limiter: recheck current load limits
      Limiter -> LoadRules: apply ordered reductions
      Limiter --> Comparison: exact fitted definitions and current-FTP metrics
      Comparison --> Applier: accepted comparison
      loop each affected planned workout
        Applier -> Editor: apply!(adapt, prepared_preview)
        Editor -> Database: save exact shown steps, metrics and generation choices
      end
      opt accepted global bias changes
        Applier -> Database: save clamped intensity_bias
      end
      Applier -> Database: destroy proposal
    end
  end
end
Controller --> Rider: redirect to calendar with result

note over Freshness, Database
  Completed structure, feedback and snapshots remain immutable.
  Openers record feedback without progression adaptation.
  Late feedback is suppressed if the next scheduled workout is completed.
  Freshness uses relevant canonical inputs; FTP-only metric updates do not stale it.
  Any acceptance/persistence failure rolls back the entire transaction.
end note
@enduml
